---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import AccuracyList from '../components/AccuracyList.astro';
import { LEGAL_REVISED, CONTACT_ENABLED } from '../lib/site';
const crumbs = [{ name: 'Home', href: '/' }, { name: 'Terms of use', href: '/terms/' }];
---
<Base title="Terms of Use | TireMileage" description="Terms of use for TireMileage, an informational tire-data website: use at your own risk, no warranty, third-party links, intellectual property and limitation of liability." crumbs={crumbs}>
  <h1>Terms of use</h1>
  <div class="answer"><strong>Quick answer:</strong> TireMileage is an informational website. It is provided “as is”, its content can be wrong or out of date, and you use it at your own risk. By using the site you agree to these terms.</div>
  <p class="meta">Last revised: <time datetime={LEGAL_REVISED}>{LEGAL_REVISED}</time>. These terms are a general, plain-language statement and are not legal advice.</p>

  <h2>1. Using the site</h2>
  <p>These terms apply to your use of tiremileage.com (“TireMileage”, “the site”, “we”, “us”). If you do not agree, please do not use the site. You may use the site for lawful, personal or business reference purposes. Please do not misuse it, for example by attempting to disrupt it, overload it with automated requests, or gain unauthorized access to it.</p>

  <h2>2. Informational use only; use at your own risk</h2>
  <p>The site provides general information about tires. It is not professional, safety, engineering, financial or legal advice, and it does not create any advisory relationship. You are responsible for your own decisions about buying, installing, maintaining and replacing tires, and you use the site and its content at your own risk.</p>

  <h2 id="data-accuracy">3. Data accuracy and safety</h2>
  <p>Please read this together with our stand-alone <a href="/disclaimer/">Disclaimer</a>.</p>
  <AccuracyList />

